About

    This subdirectory contains a patch that exposes AGAMA's Fortran interface to Ramses.

    IMPORTANT:
    - The AGAMA library must be compiled on the SAME system that this patch is meant to be run!
    - The *standard* AGAMA inferface is provided by linking to agama.so
    - The folder 'interface' provides a *custom* interface that shows how to add functionality to the standard interface WITHOUT the need to recompile the AGAMA library
    - The directory 'devel' was used as a development space. It has been kept for future reference and guidance.

Usage

    Compile Ramses patch with either of:

        - Makefile_AGAMA_MULTIPATCH
        - Makefile_AGAMA_DICE_MULTIPATCH

    In the NML, include the following block:

    ! file path is set by initfile (in INIT_PARAMS):
    &AGAMA_PARAMS
    agama_pot_file = 'some_agama_potential.ini'
    agama_stz_file = 'some_table_name.dat'
    agama_verbose = .false. ! (default: .true.)
    t_step = 0.0            ! controls the file read frequency (default: 1e10)
    /

    ALSO IMPORTANT: Requires gravity_type < 0

    &POISSON_PARAMS
    gravity_type=-1
    /

    Furthermore, MAY NEED TO ADJUST mass_sph in REFINE_PARAMS to match a fully responsive analogue.

    See Notes below.

Notes
    - 'agama_pot_file' is either an INI file with [Potential] section, either specifing an analytic potential or with a potential approximation and derivatives (with its coefficients, etc.)
    - 'agama_verbose' provides output to stdout about when and which INI file is read
    - the file is read at every 't_step'; the default value of t_step = 1e10 means the file is only read at t = 0.


